# Git Safety (Conditional)

## When
- Performing git operations (commit, rebase, reset, push, branch cleanup).
- Keep this rule broad even when stack-specific globs are used elsewhere.

## Do
- Keep commits scoped to one logical goal when possible.
- Write commit messages with intent (`why`) and impact.
- Request explicit confirmation before destructive operations.

## Avoid
- `git reset --hard`, force pushes, or history rewrites without explicit user approval.
- Reverting unrelated user changes.

## Done when
- Git actions are safe, scoped, and aligned with explicit user intent.
